;; base-menu-init-by-other's own real defbehavior (menu2-quartet-landing
;; rung, goal_src/jakx/engine/ui/menu2-installs.gc) now compiles before this
;; file in dgo build order, so this forward-declare is no longer load-bearing
;; for compile order, but the stale (function object vector int object)
;; shape it carried was silently downgrading the symbol's registered type
;; back from the real (function base-menu-info vector int object :behavior
;; base-menu) every time this file compiled (a define-extern warning, not an
;; error, but the old placeholder shape must not survive per that rung's own
;; STEP 3). Updated to match; kept rather than deleted so the
;; run-function-in-process/run-now-in-process call sites below stay
;; self-contained and readable without depending on this file's own compile
;; order relative to menu2-installs.gc.
(define-extern base-menu-init-by-other (function base-menu-info vector int object :behavior base-menu))

